title the trees that held real work -- mind rebases its laps home, mystery stashes its refused lap by name
prompt Keaton pasted mind's diverged refusal and mystery's dirty-worktree refusal.
think Both trees hold real work, so neither takes the discard cure. Mind diverged because its supervised laps landed local signed commits that never pushed before the hook crash: a named stash push guards loose leavings (the proven ImageEditHistory stash moves one slot down, untouched), pull --rebase carries the local commits onto the moved xy, both remotes take the push, the custody file clears, the supervisor arms -- with the conflict fallback parking the commits on a mind-parked branch and resetting to xy/main. Mystery's dirty ITINERARY and shelf index ARE its finished doorway lap, the one the broken pre-commit refused at the signer, so the cure is a stash push -u under a name that says what it holds -- the untracked session log rides in -- then the fast-forward pull and the armed loop; re-landing the stashed lap is a review task for a later sitting since its card edits would conflict with the five commits landed since.
obs The four pier and Mac refusals of this hour sort into exactly two families: copies discard (hush), real work rebases or stashes by name (dream, mind, mystery). The distinguishing question is always whether the bytes exist anywhere else.
